new file mode 100644
index 0000000..59a1339
--- /dev/null
+++ b/LEGACY_IOS5.md
@@ -0,0 +1,85 @@
+# Explicit legacy iOS 5 driver support
+
+`-enable-legacy-ios5-runtime` opts into the matching patched Swift frontend and
+runtime. It does not activate merely because the deployment target is old.
+Supported targets are Apple armv7 iOS devices (not armv7s, simulator, Catalyst,
+tvOS or target variants). The minimum driver deployment target becomes iOS 5;
+the normal 32-bit upper deployment restriction is unchanged. Marking-only mode
+does not lower the driver's deployment floor.
+
+The runtime implies legacy Objective-C class marking. The driver also accepts
+`-enable-legacy-ios5-class-marking` and `-disable-legacy-ios5-class-marking`;
+the last marking switch wins. Runtime plus effective disable is an error.
+Static output/runtime/resource modes are unsupported. These three options all
+participate in incremental build argument hashing.
+
+The runtime option is sent to both frontend compilation and target-info queries,
+including explicit `-print-target-info`. The host-triple query is unchanged.
+The matching frontend chooses `usr/lib/swift_ios5`, relative to the compiler,
+unless `-resource-dir` explicitly overrides it. The driver uses that returned
+resource directory for modules, runtime libraries and the legacy CRT. SDK library
+search and default system rpath use `usr/lib/swift_ios5` (explicit rpath policy
+switches retain their normal precedence).
+
+Legacy dynamic links include `-lobjc -lSystem`; existing Swift autolink and
+compatibility-library processing is retained. Executables additionally use
+`-Wl,-no_new_main` and `<resource-dir>/iphoneos/crt1.3.1.o`, with an actionable
+error if the CRT is absent. Dylibs do not receive executable startup arguments.
+Both legacy executables and dylibs also require
+`<resource-dir>/iphoneos/libswiftLegacyIOS5Backports.a`, passed as a normal archive
+input (lazy extraction, never force-loaded). Missing archives produce an
+actionable install/build error; absent-flag links do not require the archive.
+Build it from the Swift fork's `utils/legacy-ios5-mac/LegacyRuntimeBackports.c` for
+armv7 iOS 5. The current backport reproduces upstream Swift 5.10's
+`swift_stdlib_isStackAllocationSafe` implementation: return false to select the
+real heap fallback, not an invented stack-safety check.
+The CRT must actually be a correctly built armv7 iOS 5 startup object; an empty
+file is not a usable runtime. `-no_new_main` requests the legacy UNIXTHREAD
+startup path; verifying the resulting Mach-O load commands is still required.
+
+## Option source and regeneration
+
+`Sources/SwiftOptions/Options.swift` is checked-in generated code. The canonical
+source is the compiler's `include/swift/Option/Options.td`, not a driver-local
+TableGen file. The corresponding three definitions have been synchronized by
+hand here because no supported Swift host compiler or generated Options.inc is
+available in this environment. With the matching patched compiler's generated
+headers available, follow the repository's normal generation process:
+
+```sh
+swift build -Xcc -I/path/to/compiler-build/include --product makeOptions
+.build/debug/makeOptions > Sources/SwiftOptions/Options.swift
+```
+
+Review regenerated output for unrelated upstream option drift. Do not mark these
+options `DoesNotAffectIncrementalBuild` in either tree.
+
+## Build dependencies and validation
+
+A host Swift toolchain supporting the package's Swift tools version 5.7 is
+required (Swift 5.10 recommended), including SwiftPM and XCTest. Swift 5.1.5 is
+too old. A C/C++ compiler and normal host build tools are needed for llbuild,
+Yams and the option generator. No Apple SDK is required for the focused
+in-memory unit tests:
+
+```sh
+swift test --filter LegacyIOS5Tests
+```
+
+SwiftPM dependencies declared by Package.swift are swift-llbuild release/5.10,
+swift-tools-support-core release/5.10, Yams 5.0.x, swift-argument-parser 1.2.x,
+and transitive swift-system. Alternatively SWIFTCI_USE_LOCAL_DEPS uses the
+existing sibling llbuild, swift-tools-support-core, yams and
+swift-argument-parser directories; provisioning them is outside this patch.
+The checked-in Package.resolved has main-branch pins for llbuild/TSC that differ
+from the manifest's release/5.10 requirements; do not assume it is an exact
+release/5.10 lockfile without checking SwiftPM resolution.
+
+Only `git diff --check` and source review were performed here: neither `swift`
+nor `swiftc` is on PATH. Unit tests and actual frontend integration tests remain
+pending. The test suite covers parsing/incremental attributes, explicit opt-in,
+unsupported target/mode validation, deployment-floor isolation, target-info
+forwarding/explicit resource overrides, library paths/rpaths, missing CRT, and
+executable-versus-dylib startup flags. Actual armv7 compile/link, Mach-O
+UNIXTHREAD inspection, and real iOS 5 device execution remain pending. No Mac
+access, builds, other repository changes or commits are part of this work.
